<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hmannan Yazawin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1832</span> · Also known as Glass Palace Chronicle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hmannan Yazawin, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gla">Glass</a> Palace Chronicle, is the official chronicle of the Burmese monarchy, compiled by a committee of scholars appointed by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagyidaw">Bagyidaw</a> in 1829 and completed in 1832. Drawing on earlier chronicles and inscriptions, it narrates the history of the Burmese kings from legendary origins to 1821, and it remained the standard account of Burmese history into the twentieth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hmannan-yazawin.jpg" alt="Hmannan Yazawin" width="320" height="546" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hybernator · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Glass_Palace_Chronicle.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
